568	    <div class="prose">
569	      <p class="intro">Computing, technology, and artificial intelligence now shape how we learn, work, communicate, and make decisions. This course helps you meet that world on your own terms.</p>
570	      <p>Across the term you'll use computing as a tool to work and create with data; learn effectively — with and without AI; find and judge digital information; reason about the ethics of technology; and build a professional digital presence for your career. It's designed for students of every background, and assumes no prior experience.</p>
571	      <p>Each week centers on a short <b>discussion</b> — a post and a reply that connect the week's ideas to real situations — and the term builds toward three hands-on assignments. There are no exams; you learn by making, evaluating, and reflecting.</p>
